From 4427283d825678e2f2ec37a1551edb0e51030b2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Pin the remaining requests of a provider to its uplink

Three requests of a provider with an uplink still left over the
default route: the status check of a cached playlist or EPG file,
the web page a web stream's URL is extracted from, and UDP and RTP
streams. Stamp the uplink on the status check and on UDP and RTP
stream URLs, except the udpxy relay URLs multicast streams are
rewritten to, and hand the stream URL's uplink options to the page
fetch.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
